"rempel@gmail.com" schrieb:
> 
> Hey all - I am a devotee of the original nethack. One main reason is
> that in Nethack 2.2 and later, you can only cast a spell a certain
> number of times before it wears out.

Was that different pre-2.2?

The earliest versions i played were some of the earlier 3.0s, so i
don't know for sure. In the first version i seriously played, 3.1.3,
you only got a limited number of castings out of a successful read,
but the spellbook would stay around when read and would take several
readings before it wore out.

Sometime in the 3.2 or 3.3 releases, the new spellcasting system was
introduced, with casting skills, detailed failure chances (it was
always fail or always succeed before) and spell decay was set to 20k
turns, instead of the old "limited number of castings" rule, that had
made casters and spells very weak in older versions.

> Is there anything you can do to
> "refresh" a spell?

Read the spellbook again - either the old one, or acquire a new one.

> What's the point of a spellbook if you can't keep
> the spell and the spellbook disappears after you read it?

That's a good reason to upgrade to a more recent version, in which
spellbooks don't generally disappear upon reading.

